                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237985156",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199786100835",
                            "num_reviews": 6,
                            "playtime_forever": 265,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 258,
                            "last_played": 1792546812
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I never heard of this game before, just found it across some game recommendations from what i can possibly remember, when I finished this very game I actually completely fell in love with it, the pixelated art towards the soundtrack, scenery, and the overall theme and setting really hit. This is a game where if you want to play something like just a very relaxing and slow pixelated story game, this is one of those games entirely as far as that goes, anyone can easily fall in love with this game as the touching and heartfelt storytelling with some pretty funny hilarious moments really makes you feel at home, I specifically say that because the game is about traveling and exploring an ancient civilization and various \"sights\" that are flashbacks from the past, and you explore through various ruins and even roaming in an alternate world, by the time you start and even finish this game you feel not only complete in a way, but the journey this game takes you through is like a completely astonished and beautiful scenery to feel bestowed upon.",
